<article class="env-definition" id="0FZT">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FZT">Definition <span data-tag="0FZT">57.10.1</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. Let $\mathcal{D}$ be a triangulated category. We say two exact functors of triangulated categories </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  F, F' : D^ b(\mathcal{A}) \longrightarrow \mathcal{D}  \]
</div>
  <p> are <em>siblings</em>, or we say $F'$ is a <em>sibling</em> of $F$, if the following two conditions are satisfied </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
the functors $F \circ i$ and $F' \circ i$ are isomorphic where $i : \mathcal{A} \to D^ b(\mathcal{A})$ is the inclusion functor, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$F(K) \cong F'(K)$ for any $K$ in $D^ b(\mathcal{A})$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>